{"kind":"assert","text":"C4 one submit, item 3 of 77a253b9: the call shape and the changed paths, before any apply. Source only; nothing is applied or compiled.\n\nValue. `DraftNow {key, kind, address, head, primary: ActRef|null, subjects}` has one key per expected name of the act (`selectDraftSubjects` names). Each key holds `{is:\"present\", ref}` or `{is:\"absent\"}`, so the primary and every `also` and `via` are covered. `primary` is null only for an open act or a comment on null. Both return forms carry `now`. The view computes it and stores nothing.\n\nClient. `submit(slot, now?)`. The call copies and checks the value before its first await. Under the fence it applies `taken`/`state` first, then the `shape` checks: a returned draft with a missing, ill-shaped or foreign `now` stops, and so does an editing draft that is given one. It then builds the candidate in memory with `expected` from `now`, runs Explore (a moved subject gives form 1 and no signature), writes one member batch that adopts the refs, and retains and signs. No `shape` stop reaches the write or the signature.\n\nMCP. A kept refused request's `act` and `settle` results gain `now {of, target, kind, primary, at, head}`. The `act` tool gains `after` and `now` as a pair, with `at` absent. A missing or foreign pair stops with `shape` before `signedIntent`. A bare `act` stays a fresh act.\n\nChanged paths. New `packages/client/src/draft-now.ts` and `packages/client/src/draft-submit.ts`. Checkpoint files `draft-project-types.ts` and `draft-project.ts`. `scope-client.ts` and `scope.ts`, which the constructor prefix also touches: this change composes after the prefix and the whole-batch loader. `packages/mcp/src/shape.ts`, `service.ts`, `input-schema.ts`, `act-result.ts`, plus `docs/mcp-tools.json`, `docs/mcp.md`, and your seventh amendment.\n\nCallers that cannot hold the view. The Page (`apps/room/page/src/data.ts:1477`) owns no `scopeClient` today; it can pass `now` once it owns one. The generic MCP `act` keeps no draft store, so the model must copy `now` back; a host that drops tool output gets `shape`. The CLI runs one fresh act per process and needs no `now`. `hosted.ts` signs only `enrol` (:1504); I found no second generic act path there.\n\nQuestions:\n1. Form 1: keep the cut stored with the movement (proposed), or recompute at view?\n2. A returned draft whose primary row lies outside the checked cut has no `now`: stop with `state`?\n3. Does `after` plus `now` count on MCP as \"a draft whose view holds `now`\"?\n4. `now` on every refused MCP result, or only on `revision-moved`?\n5. A scope refusal after Explore returns form 2 again with a new `now`, and needs one more submit with no hidden retry. Confirm?","body":{"hold":"Compile hold 22ed0d6c stands: no apply or compile before your word. Form 2, B1 and member-only writes stay; no hidden autofill or background write. The step 5 candidate never takes Explore.result.act.","proposal":"/private/tmp/artroom-c4-general-now-call-shape-20261116/PROPOSAL.md 13565 B SHA fc95e1b4191647b1a90f6d4363f0d45e6b07743541bf83ea6c52a8b4b1744118; bindings.json binds every cited file","tests":"New packages/client/test/c4-draft-now.test.ts (12 cases, one per decision row, including the 39-to-40 race and a moved also subject); extensions to packages/mcp/test/captured-revisions.scope.test.ts and shape.test.ts (6 cases)."}}